config BR2_PACKAGE_TAQ102_WIFI
	bool "taq102-wifi (RTL8723CS driver and bring-up)"
	select BR2_PACKAGE_WPA_SUPPLICANT
	select BR2_PACKAGE_WPA_SUPPLICANT_NL80211
	select BR2_PACKAGE_WPA_SUPPLICANT_CLI
	select BR2_PACKAGE_WPA_SUPPLICANT_PASSPHRASE
	help
	  The stock RTL8723CS module taken off this device, plus the script
	  that loads it and brings wlan0 up from a configuration on /data.

	  The module is the vendor's own binary rather than a rebuild: the
	  stock kernel is built with CONFIG_MODVERSIONS=y, so any rebuilt
	  kernel would have to reproduce both the vermagic string and every
	  symbol CRC before it would load.
